{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Gad, a troop</b> etc. He enfolds his blessing in his name, for the meaning of ״Gad״ is in the sense of troop (gedud), meaning camp, and in the sense of kid (gediyah), and in the sense of drawing/pulling (meshichah), and in the sense of surrounding (heikef), for all are contained in the meaning of ״Gad״; see the Aruch under the entry ״Gad.״ And he says <b>Gad, a troop (gedud)</b> — his enemies will surround him at his borders, <b>and he will troop (yagud)</b> — meaning he will cut them down. ״Akev״ means until extermination. Further, it intends <b>gedud</b> in the sense of camp, that his troops will multiply and his camp will keep advancing, and this is what he said ״yagudenu,״ and his saying <b>and he will troop (yagud)</b> means he will surround the entire camp of Israel and wage war on their behalf. ״Akev״ means until they inherit all their inheritance (Numbers 32:32)."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:40.514292364Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}